Database migrations
===================

Run commands from backend/ with the same DATABASE_URL as the deployed service.
Back up an existing database before migration. Production startup does not
create, seed, or silently alter tables.

Empty database:
    ./venv/bin/python -m alembic upgrade head

Existing pre-migration database:
    1. Back up the database.
    2. Verify its tables/columns/constraints match 0001_baseline.py. Do not stamp
       an empty database, a partially migrated database, or an unknown schema.
    3. ./venv/bin/python -m alembic stamp 0001
    4. ./venv/bin/python -m alembic upgrade head

Development databases created from the current models already include
DailyReadiness. Verify the full schema before stamping head instead.

Verification:
    ./venv/bin/python -m alembic current
    ./venv/bin/python -m alembic check

A Docker image includes these scripts. Run `alembic upgrade head` once as a
release job before starting the application containers. Do not run concurrent
schema migrations from multiple replicas. Deployment of an old, unstamped
production database requires the adoption steps above.

0001: original schema (including password reset, messaging, and financial data)
0002: daily_readiness, keyed by user and Asia/Tehran calendar day

Downgrading 0002 deletes stored readiness data. Restore a backup when rollback
must preserve it. Backups and adoption are operator actions, not automatic
startup side effects.
